{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Intervals","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecificLimits.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.no_continuous_evaluation_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.no_continuous_evaluation_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.lean#L208-L217","doc":"**Contrapositive, as used.** If a real point admits the limit that a\ncontinuous evaluation of the completion requires, it is not `> 1`.\n\nThe substrate anchor `q₀ ≈ 1.10998` satisfies `1 < q₀`, so `qou-qb8e` item 1 —\n\"a Habiro-ring element whose archimedean evaluation at `q₀` reproduces `c₃`\" —\nasks for the value of an object that has none at that point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch_not_tendsto_zero_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch_not_tendsto_zero_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.lean#L174-L206","doc":"**No archimedean evaluation at real `q > 1`.**\n\nA continuous evaluation of the cyclotomic completion at a point `q` requires\n`(q;q)ₙ → 0`, since `(q;q)ₙ → 0` holds in the completion itself. For real\n`q > 1` that limit fails: the moduli are eventually non-decreasing and bounded\nbelow by the (nonzero) modulus at the index where `q ^ (n+1) ≥ 2` first holds.\n\nStated with that index as an explicit hypothesis `N`, so the proof is elementary\nand the statement is exactly what is used downstream. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch_abs_le_succ_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch_abs_le_succ_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.lean#L163-L172","doc":"**The modulus is eventually non-decreasing.** Once `q ^ (n+1) ≥ 2` — which\nfor real `q > 1` holds from some index on — the step from `n` to `n+1` cannot\nshrink `|(q;q)ₙ|`. The `q > 1` hypothesis is not needed separately: it is already\ncarried by `2 ≤ q ^ (n+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.one_le_abs_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.one_le_abs_factor","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.lean#L153-L161","doc":"For real `q > 1` and `k ≥ 1` with `q ^ k ≥ 2`, the factor has modulus `≥ 1`.\n\n`q ^ k ≥ 2` holds for all large `k` since `q > 1`; the hypothesis is carried\nexplicitly so the lemma stays elementary. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch_ne_zero_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch_ne_zero_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.lean#L142-L151","doc":"For real `q > 1`, every factor `1 - q^k` with `k ≥ 1` is nonzero, so\n`(q;q)ₙ ≠ 0` for all `n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch_eq_zero_of_pow_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch_eq_zero_of_pow_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.lean#L120-L138","doc":"At a root of unity of order `N ≥ 1`, `(q;q)ₙ` vanishes for every `n ≥ N`:\nthe `k = N` factor is `1 - q^N = 0`. Generic (`CommRing`).\n\nThis is the *positive* half of the trichotomy — it is exactly why the cyclotomic\ncompletion is built at roots of unity, and why a Habiro element has honest values\nthere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch_reflection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch_reflection","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.lean#L89-L116","doc":"**The reflection identity.**\n`(q⁻¹;q⁻¹)ₙ = (-1)^n · q^(-(n(n+1)/2)) · (q;q)ₙ`, written multiplicatively as\n\n  `q ^ (∑ k in range n, (k+1)) * (q⁻¹;q⁻¹)ₙ = (-1)^n * (q;q)ₙ`\n\nto stay inside the ring (no negative exponents). The exponent\n`∑_{k<n} (k+1) = n(n+1)/2` is the blow-up factor: for `|q| > 1` it is exactly\nwhat separates the divergent branch from the convergent one.\n\nGeneric — any field, `q ≠ 0`. No ordering, no `ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.one_sub_inv_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.one_sub_inv_pow","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.lean#L79-L87","doc":"**Termwise reflection.** For `q ≠ 0` in a field,\n`1 - q⁻ᵏ = -q⁻ᵏ * (1 - q^k)`, the single algebraic fact the whole trichotomy\nrests on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch_succ","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.lean#L74-L75","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch_zero","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.lean#L72-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.qPoch","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/HabiroEvaluationTrichotomy.lean#L64-L70","doc":"The `q`-Pochhammer symbol `(q;q)ₙ = ∏_{k=1}^{n} (1 - q^k)`.\n\nGeneric in the base ring: this is pure `CommRing` data, with no ordering and no\narchimedean input, per the §7c base-ring convention. ","signatureChunk":0}]}